{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":28572,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,8]],"date-time":"2025-09-08T06:02:29Z","timestamp":1757311349955,"version":"3.37.3"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,17]]},"group-title":"ENGINEERING","reference-count":0,"publisher":"MDPI AG","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,17]],"date-time":"2022-05-17T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1652745600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"accepted":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,16]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Fundamental science and applied research and technology development (RTD) are facing significant challenges that particularly compound to the notorious credibility, reproducibility, funding and sustainability crises. The underlying, serious shortcomings are substantially amplified by a metrics-obsessed publication culture, and a growing cohort of academics fishing for fairly stagnant (public) funding budgets. This work presents, for the first time, a groundbreaking strategy to successfully address these severe issues; the novel strategy proposed here leverages the distributed ledger technology (DLT) &amp;ldquo;blockchain&amp;rdquo; to capitalize on cryptoeconomic mechanisms, such as tokenization, consensus, crowdsourcing, smart contracts, reputation systems as well as staking, reward and slashing mechanisms. This powerful toolbox, which is so far widely unfamiliar to traditional scientific and RTD communities (&amp;ldquo;TradSci&amp;rdquo;), is synergistically combined with the exponentially growing computing capabilities for virtualizing experiments through digital twin methods in a future scientific &amp;ldquo;metaverse&amp;rdquo;. Project contributions, such as hypotheses, methods, experimental data, modelling, simulation, assessment, predictions and directions are crowdsourced using blockchain, and captured by so-called non-fungible tokens (&amp;ldquo;NFTs&amp;rdquo;). The so enabled, highly integrative approach, termed decentralized science (&amp;ldquo;DeSci&amp;rdquo;), is destined to move research out of its present silos, and to markedly enhance quality, credibility, efficiency, transparency, inclusiveness, sustainability, impact, and sustainability of a wide spectrum of academic and commercial research initiatives.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.20944\/preprints202205.0223.v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,17]],"date-time":"2022-05-17T07:19:51Z","timestamp":1652771991000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":4,"title":["DeSci-Decentralized Science"],"prefix":"10.20944","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0366-1897","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jens","family":"Ducr\u00e9e","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Martin","family":"Codyre","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ray","family":"Walshe","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"S\u00f6nke","family":"Barting","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"1968","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,17]],"date-time":"2022-05-17T07:20:15Z","timestamp":1652772015000},"score":34.16429,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.preprints.org\/manuscript\/202205.0223\/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,17]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.20944\/preprints202205.0223.v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2022,5,17]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,4,1]],"date-time":"2025-04-01T06:24:55Z","timestamp":1743488695240},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,23]]},"group-title":"Computer Science and Mathematics","reference-count":0,"publisher":"MDPI AG","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,23]],"date-time":"2024-01-23T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1705968000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"accepted":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,22]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Background: Rapid advancements in Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT), including blockchain, are foundational to a new era of digital innovation. This innovation has catalyzed the emergence of &amp;lsquo;Decentralized Science (DeSci),&amp;rsquo; a new concept and movement that aims to address the challenges of modern science. Objective: Given the novelty of the field of DeSci, this study aims to provide a comprehensive definition of the term as well as explore and conceptualize shared values and guiding principles inherent to DeSci. Methods: In line with the objectives of this study, an exploratory literature review was conducted to identify and synthesize the scholarly and secondary literature. The search and selection process included six databases (PubMed, Google Scholar, Web of Science, IEEE Xplore, arXiv, and Social Science Research Network), and the search period was limited to the last 15 years, from 2008 to 2023. To identify relevant secondary literature, such as articles, reports, blog posts, and website content, a keyword search was conducted in three search engines (Google.com, Bing.com, and Yahoo.com). Owing to the novelty of the concept and movement of DeSci, the exploratory literature review was supplemented by an anonymous online-based expert survey using a combination of single-choice and open-ended questions. The experts were selected based on predefined inclusion criteria, in association with their activities in the field of DeSci. The responses to the single-choice questions were subject to statistical analysis, whereas the open-ended questions were analyzed using qualitative content analysis. Results: Seven studies were selected for evaluation as part of the search and selection process to identify relevant scholarly literature. Following the review of secondary literature, additional 24 publications were included in the analysis. In the expert survey, 39 valid datasets were collected and analyzed. Following the synthesis of the results of the exploratory literature review and expert survey, a comprehensive definition of the term &amp;lsquo;Decentralized Science&amp;rsquo; (DeSci) was formulated to reflect recurring themes. As no publications that explicitly discussed or addressed the values or principles of DeSci in the exploratory literature review could be identified, a set of shared values and guiding principles for DeSci were defined based on the results of the expert survey. Conclusion: The results of this study underscore the emerging nature of DeSci, as evidenced by the limited availability of relevant information and scarcity of academic publications. While this study proposes a comprehensive definition of DeSci as well as a set of shared values and guiding principles, the results of this study highlight the importance of ongoing evaluation and validation. Furthermore, the results of this study indicate a clear need for future research in the field of DeSci, emphasizing its dynamic and developing nature.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.20944\/preprints202401.1638.v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,24]],"date-time":"2024-01-24T09:07:26Z","timestamp":1706087246000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Decentralized Science (DeSci): Definition, Shared Values, and Guiding Principles"],"prefix":"10.20944","author":[{"given":"Lukas","family":"Weidener","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"1968","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,30]],"date-time":"2024-07-30T11:14:37Z","timestamp":1722338077000},"score":32.83705,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.preprints.org\/manuscript\/202401.1638\/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,23]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.20944\/preprints202401.1638.v1","relation":{"is-preprint-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.3389\/fbloc.2024.1375763","asserted-by":"subject"}]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,23]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,12]],"date-time":"2026-06-12T16:03:47Z","timestamp":1781280227046,"version":"3.54.1"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,27]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,27]],"date-time":"2025-06-27T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1750982400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by-nc-sa\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Data labeling is a critical, yet resource-intensive process for machine learning applications. Traditional centralized platforms face challenges in terms of scalability, payment processing, and quality control. This study presents a decentralized data labeling platform that leverages the Solana blockchain for transparent and efficient micropayments. Our system combines crowdbased image annotation with blockchain-enabled payments and implements a voting mechanism for quality assurance. The platform utilizes Next.js for front-end development and Node.js for back-end services, and integrates AWS S3 for storage with Solana smart contracts for payment processing. Performance evaluation demonstrated low transaction costs, rapid payment confirmation, and scalability to handle 1000+ concurrent users. Our approach eliminates intermediaries, reduces payment delays from weeks to seconds, and provides transparent verification using blockchain transactions.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.36227\/techrxiv.175100033.39587420\/v1","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,27]],"date-time":"2025-06-27T00:59:01Z","timestamp":1750985941000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Decentralized Data Labeling with Solana-Driven Micropayments"],"prefix":"10.36227","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0004-0683-0723","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Adarsh","family":"Sinha","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Engineering North Eastern Regional Institute of Science and Technology Nirjuli"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ajit Kumar Singh","family":"Yadav","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Engineering North Eastern Regional Institute of Science and Technology Nirjuli"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"263","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.techrxiv.org\/doi\/pdf\/10.36227\/techrxiv.175100033.39587420\/v1","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,12]],"date-time":"2026-06-12T15:27:26Z","timestamp":1781278046000},"score":30.790728,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.techrxiv.org\/doi\/full\/10.36227\/techrxiv.175100033.39587420\/v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,27]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.36227\/techrxiv.175100033.39587420\/v1","published":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,27]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,8]],"date-time":"2024-10-08T04:24:19Z","timestamp":1728361459410},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":10,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.4950696","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,7]],"date-time":"2024-10-07T19:15:57Z","timestamp":1728328557000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Adapting Mintzberg's Organizational Theory to DeSci: The Decentralized Science Pyramid Framework"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Lukas","family":"Weidener","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Konrad","family":"Greilich","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Mark","family":"Melnykowycz","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"78","reference":[{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.3389\/fbloc.2024.1375763","article-title":"Decentralized Science (DeSci): Definition, Shared Values, and Guiding Principles","volume":"7","author":"L Weidener","year":"2024","journal-title":"Frontiers in Blockchain"},{"key":"ref2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1563","DOI":"10.1109\/TCSS.2022.3204745","article-title":"DeSci Based on Web3 and DAO: A Comprehensive Overview and Reference Model","volume":"9","author":"W Ding","year":"2022","journal-title":"IEEE Trans Comput Soc Syst"},{"key":"ref3","author":"P Mayr","year":"2022","journal-title":"The Emerging DeSci Stack"},{"key":"ref4","author":"H Mintzberg","year":"1979","journal-title":"The Structuring of Organizations: A Synthesis of Research"},{"key":"ref5","author":"J Song","year":"2021","journal-title":"Altcoins are DINOs (Decentralized in Name Only)"},{"key":"ref6","first-page":"135","article-title":"Company Law and Autonomous Systems: A Blueprint for Lawyers, Entrepreneurs, and Regulators","author":"S Bayern","year":"2017","journal-title":"Hastings Science and Technology Law Journal"},{"key":"ref7","author":"R Lamberty","journal-title":"Efficiency in Digital Economies -A Primer on Tokenomics"},{"key":"ref8","author":"T Golato","year":"2021","journal-title":"VitaDAO Whitepaper 1.0"},{"key":"ref9","year":"2024","journal-title":"Contribute to VitaDAO"},{"key":"ref10","author":"T White","year":"2024","journal-title":"2024 Election of Working Group Stewards"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,7]],"date-time":"2024-10-07T19:20:22Z","timestamp":1728328822000},"score":30.434372,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=4950696"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"references-count":10,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.4950696","published":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,14]],"date-time":"2026-08-14T10:32:39Z","timestamp":1786703559960,"version":"build-2736575974"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]],"date-time":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1767225600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>The article addresses the problem of speculative tokenomics in decentralized science (DeSci) projects. Based on an analysis of existing approaches (Gupta, 2025; Weidener &amp;amp; Boltz, 2025), the author identifies a key contradiction between the governance functions of a token and its role as a speculative asset. An alternative model is proposed in which the token acts as a \"digital receipt\" confirming real contribution, and governance is separated from staking. The model includes deflationary stabilization mechanisms (burning 50% of fees), three-component staking, and a community-managed grant fund. The results can be used in the design of sustainable DeSci platforms.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7272460","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,14]],"date-time":"2026-08-14T09:54:19Z","timestamp":1786701259000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["&lt;div&gt;\n The Problem of Speculative Tokenomics in Decentralized Science (DeSci) and Possible Solutions\n&lt;\/div&gt;"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-1219-2854","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Saridi Dimitriy","family":"Yuryevich","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,14]],"date-time":"2026-08-14T09:54:19Z","timestamp":1786701259000},"score":29.31495,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=7272460"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7272460","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,5]],"date-time":"2026-09-05T11:59:55Z","timestamp":1788609595692,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":79,"publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,17]],"date-time":"2024-07-17T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1721174400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["frontiersin.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Front. Blockchain"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Rapid advancements in Distributed Ledger Technology (DLT), including blockchain, are foundational to a new era of digital innovation. This innovation has catalyzed the emergence of \u201cDecentralized Science (DeSci),\u201d a new concept and movement that aims to address the challenges of modern science. Given the novelty of the field of DeSci, this study aims to provide a comprehensive definition of the term and explore and conceptualize the shared values and guiding principles inherent to DeSci. To achieve these objectives, an exploratory literature review was conducted to identify and synthesize the scholarly and secondary literature. The search and selection process included six databases (PubMed, Google Scholar, Web of Science, IEEE Xplore, arXiv, and Social Science Research Network), focusing on the last 15\u00a0years (2008 to 2023). Owing to the novelty of DeSci, the literature review was supplemented by an anonymous online-based expert survey using a combination of single-choice and open-ended questions. The experts were selected based on predefined inclusion criteria related to their activities in the DeSci field. Seven studies were selected for evaluation from the scholarly literature, and additional 24 sources of information were included in the analysis. In the expert survey, 39 valid datasets were collected and analyzed. The synthesis of the exploratory literature review and expert survey results led to a comprehensive definition of \u201cDecentralized Science\u201d (DeSci) reflecting recurring themes. As no publications explicitly discussed or addressed the values or principles of DeSci in the literature review, a set of shared values and guiding principles was defined based on the expert survey results. This study proposes a comprehensive definition of DeSci and a set of shared values and guiding principles, highlighting the importance of future research in this area.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3389\/fbloc.2024.1375763","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,17]],"date-time":"2024-07-17T01:05:04Z","timestamp":1721178304000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3389\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":26,"title":["Decentralized science (DeSci): definition, shared values, and guiding principles"],"prefix":"10.3389","volume":"7","author":[{"given":"Lukas","family":"Weidener","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Cord","family":"Spreckelsen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1965","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,17]]},"reference":[{"key":"B1","unstructured":"Is DeSci the future of research?\n            AkinoshoS.\n          2022"},{"key":"B2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"260","DOI":"10.1177\/1461444812451567","article-title":"What was Web 2.0? Versions as the dominant mode of internet history","volume":"15","author":"Allen","year":"2013","journal-title":"New Media and Soc."},{"key":"B3","volume-title":"Blockchain for science and knowledge creation","author":"Bartling","year":"2016"},{"key":"B4","volume-title":"Mastering blockchain","author":"Bashir","year":"2017"},{"key":"B5","unstructured":"What is decentralized science (DeSci) and what makes it special?\n            BelovaK.\n          2022"},{"key":"B6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"34","DOI":"10.1038\/scientificamerican0501-34","article-title":"THE SEMANTIC WEB","volume":"284","author":"Berners-Lee","year":"2001","journal-title":"Sci. Am."},{"key":"B7","unstructured":"Decentralized science2023"},{"key":"B8","volume-title":"Science literacy: concepts, contexts, and consequences","author":"Boyd","year":"2016"},{"key":"B9","unstructured":"Science | definition, disciplines, and facts | britannica2023"},{"key":"B10","unstructured":"A next-generation smart contract and decentralized application platform\n            ButerinV.\n          2014"},{"key":"B11","unstructured":"Decentralization | English meaning - Cambridge dictionary"},{"key":"B12","unstructured":"Principle | English meaning - Cambridge dictionary"},{"key":"B13","unstructured":"Science | English meaning - Cambridge dictionary"},{"key":"B14","unstructured":"Value | English meaning - Cambridge dictionary"},{"key":"B15","unstructured":"DeSci - decentralised Science and its potential to change the world2022"},{"key":"B16","unstructured":"DeSci: the case for decentralised science\n            CookJ.\n          2021"},{"key":"B17","article-title":"Longevity startup VitaDAO raises $4","author":"Cumbers","year":"2023","journal-title":"1m, Backed By Pfizer, Balaji Srinivasan"},{"key":"B18","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.55277\/ResearchHub.8c7ndflk","volume-title":"Removing the barriers for participation in decentralized science from traditional academia","author":"Dehouche","year":"2023"},{"key":"B19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1563","DOI":"10.1109\/TCSS.2022.3204745","article-title":"DeSci based on Web3 and DAO: a